// spec: DCL-006
//
// compiled: no
//
// ⚠️ Opted out of the compiled half because the compiled back end does NOT
// have this defect -- it already hoists.  A defect present in only one
// processor cannot be recorded while the harness compares the two, and the
// recording here is the interpreted behaviour, which is the one at fault.
//
// DCL-006 makes a top-level function or class visible throughout its file, so
// this program must print 'called' and then true.  The interpreter binds the
// name when the declaration runs, so the call above it fails.
//
// ⚠️ The compiled back end already does what the rule requires.  It also hoists
// VARIABLES, which DCL-016 forbids -- see C-10.  This defect must not be fixed
// by adopting the compiler's behaviour wholesale.

Greet ();

function Greet (); begin WriteLn ('called'); end
